    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "The player chose 'Spider' as the creature type for Cavern of Souls, but 'Spider' is not even among the available choices (the options are Druid, Spirit, Elf, Noble, Horror, Avatar, Vampire, Dragon, Demon, Elder). More importantly, looking at the hand, the player has Town Greeter (Human Citizen), Oblivious Bookworm (Human Wizard), Gran-Gran (Human Peasant Ally), and Superior Spider-Man (Spider Human Hero). Choosing 'Human' would allow Cavern of Souls to cast three creatures from hand with uncounterable colored mana, while 'Spider' would only help Superior Spider-Man. The reasoning mentions Spider isn't in the top 10 but says 'I will declare it anyway' — however the game requires choosing from the presented options. Since the actual choice isn't shown as resolved, but the reasoning clearly indicates a suboptimal creature type even if it were available. Among the actual choices presented, none perfectly match, but Human isn't listed either. The player should have chosen whichever type best supports their hand — likely none of these are ideal, but the reasoning about wanting Spider over Human is clearly wrong given the hand composition.",
      "action_taken": "Attempted to choose 'Spider' as the creature type for Cavern of Souls (which may not even be a valid selection from the presented choices).",
      "better_line": "Choose a creature type that actually appears in the available options. Among the hand's creatures, 'Human' would have been the best choice if available since it covers Town Greeter, Oblivious Bookworm, and Superior Spider-Man. Since the available choices don't include Human or Spider, the player should pick whichever type is most likely to be relevant for future draws.",
      "type": "blunder",
