    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "With Gran-Gran on the opponent's board (draws a card when tapped), casting Oblivious Bookworm on turn 2 would develop a 2/3 body that provides card advantage at end step, which is arguably stronger than Town Greeter's 1/1 body with mill 4. However, Town Greeter helps find lands and fill the graveyard for Superior Spider-Man, so this is debatable. The bigger question is whether Bitter Triumph should be considered to remove Gran-Gran before it generates value — Gran-Gran's cost reduction ability with Lessons in graveyard could be very dangerous, and it draws cards whenever it taps. Using Bitter Triumph now (discarding a card) would remove a key engine piece, though it costs a card from hand.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Town Greeter for 1G",
      "better_line": "Consider casting Bitter Triumph targeting Gran-Gran to remove the opponent's card advantage engine before it generates value, or at minimum cast Oblivious Bookworm as a stronger 2/3 body that also provides card advantage. Town Greeter is reasonable but likely the weakest of the three options.",
      "type": "blunder",
