    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "The player has 2 mana available (Cavern of Souls + Starting Town) and could cast Oblivious Bookworm (costs {G}{U}). Starting Town can pay 1 life for any color, giving green, and Cavern of Souls was likely set to a creature type. However, looking more carefully: Cavern of Souls adds {C} or colored mana only for the chosen creature type. If the chosen type matches Bookworm's types (Human/Wizard), then Cavern could add {U} for it. Starting Town can add any color for 1 life, providing {G}. So casting Oblivious Bookworm was likely possible and would develop the board with a 2/3 that draws cards each end step. Holding up Bitter Triumph sounds reasonable defensively, but Bitter Triumph costs {1}{B} — the player cannot actually cast it with just Cavern of Souls and Starting Town since Cavern only adds colored mana for creature spells of the chosen type, and Bitter Triumph is not a creature spell. So the reasoning about holding up Bitter Triumph is flawed. The player should have deployed Oblivious Bookworm to develop their board, as they cannot actually use the mana for removal anyway.",
